(Summary, written by PutiaCNC)
(Zero:                   XY0 = lower-left corner of stock, Z0 = top surface, in G56)
(Start:                  Starts the spindle at 12000 rpm, then moves to X20.344 Y3.54.)
(Tools:                  3 mm flat end mill, 6 mm flat end mill. The program pauses 1 time for)
(                        you to change the tool -to 6 mm-.)
(At a tool change (!):   Touch off Z0 again with the new tool before you resume: the controller)
(                        does not know how long each tool is.)
(Cutting:                Down to Z -1 mm. 94 mm of cutting, about 11 s in all.)
(End:                    Lifts to Z 5 mm, stops the spindle, goes to X0 Y0.)
